# Haskell backend (external, protocol 2) — Bazel migration Phase 5.
#
# The emitter runs *out of process* over the emit protocol (spec/protocol.md §2):
# the `sudo_external_backend` rule pipes `sudoc emit-ir` (wrapped in the emit
# request envelope) into this sh_binary, which runs `runghc Emit.hs` and writes a
# `{files}` response that `emit_unpack` unpacks into the generated tree. Emit.hs
# imports SudoJson.hs and `readFile "SudoRt.hs"` relative to cwd, so emit.sh cd's
# to the directory holding all three .hs siblings first.
#
# hs codegen shells out to the host GHC (`runghc`), not a Bazel toolchain, so the
# rule runs it as a no-sandbox `local` action inheriting host PATH. It is an
# sh_binary, NOT a haskell_binary — rules_haskell stays out of scope (design §9).
# The runtime-discovery manifest (hs.sudoc-backend.json), `--external`, and
# `discovered_backends()` were deleted in Phase 5 Task 3.

sh_binary(
    name = "emitter",
    srcs = ["emit.sh"],
    data = [
        "Emit.hs",
        "SudoJson.hs",
        "SudoRt.hs",
    ],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
